      "adjusted_severity": "Critical",
      "reviewer_notes": "All 3 gates passed. Gate 1 skipped (missing-validation exception: the issue is the absence of a startup guard, not a dead function). Gate 2: entry point is the public HTTP `GET /oauth/userinfo` endpoint \u2014 untrusted; no trust_assumptions field present in BUG_BOUNTY_SCOPE.json to dispute. Gate 3: `src/lib/oauth.ts` is not in the out-of-scope list; OAuth token handling is an explicitly listed key security concern. An attacker can trigger this via the public `GET /oauth/userinfo` endpoint by crafting a JWT signed with the well-known hardcoded secret `'your-secret-key-change-in-production'` (visible at `src/lib/oauth.ts:L11` in the public repository), causing `verifyAccessToken()` to accept the forged token and return an arbitrary fabricated identity with attacker-controlled `sub`, `discord_id`, and `scope`.",
